# Copy to core/.env and fill in. That file is gitignored; this one is not, so never
# put a real value here.
#
# A real environment variable beats this file, so `ARIA_VOICE=af_nicole uv run …`
# still works for a one-off.

# --- Discord -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Developer Portal → your app → Bot → Reset Token. Three dot-separated parts.
# Anyone holding this can read every message the bot can see, so treat it like a
# password: if it has ever been pasted into a chat window, an issue, or a terminal
# someone else can scroll back through, reset it.
#
# Needs the MESSAGE CONTENT INTENT switched on in the same portal page. Without it
# she connects, sees your messages arrive, and finds them empty.
#
# Having a token is what turns Discord on. There is no separate enable flag.
ARIA_DISCORD_TOKEN=

# Your own Discord user id — right-click yourself → Copy User ID (needs Developer
# Mode on, under Settings → Advanced).
#
# Anyone who shares a server with the bot can open a DM to it, so this is the only
# thing tying a message to you. Set it and she answers you and nobody else, anywhere.
#
# Leave it empty and she still chats — but two things are then refused for everybody,
# you included: looking at the screen, and writing to her memory (both "remember
# that…" and the background note-taker). A planted note is the quiet one: written
# once, read back weeks later with total confidence and no idea where it came from.
ARIA_DISCORD_OWNER=

# Let other people in your servers talk to her (1 to enable, empty or 0 for off).
#
# They get a different Aria, and the separation is structural rather than a rule she
# is asked to follow: a public turn is built from its own persona and its own
# per-channel conversation, and is never handed your history, your notes, your
# continuity or the screen. She cannot discuss you because she is never given
# anything about you.
#
# Your DMs are never public, whatever this is set to. Anyone sharing a server with
# the bot can open one, so a public DM would be a private channel with a stranger in
# it. Note that a *server channel* is public even when you are the one talking in it
# — the room decides who she is, not the person, which is what stops your notes
# turning up in front of your friends.
ARIA_DISCORD_PUBLIC=

# Channels where she answers everything rather than only when @mentioned.
# Comma-separated ids: right-click a channel -> Copy Channel ID.
ARIA_DISCORD_CHANNELS=

# --- Cloud conversation model (only "Start Aria (cloud).bat" reads these) ------
# "Start Aria.bat" runs everything locally and needs none of this.
#
# What you are trading: a much larger model that follows the persona better, in
# exchange for a slower first token, a metered allowance, and everything she is told
# leaving the machine - including her notes about you, which live in the system
# prompt. Memory extraction stays local either way.
#
# Which service. Fill in the matching key below.
#   groq        30/min, 1000/day on 70B models. Fastest and most generous.
#   google      best models; the FREE tier says content is used to improve Google's
#               products. Paid tiers are excluded from that. Her notes go in the
#               system prompt, so this is a real trade rather than a footnote.
#   openrouter  widest model choice, 20/min and only 50/day (1000 if the account has
#               ever bought $10 of credit).
# Leave this commented out to use the local model via Ollama, which is the default.
# ARIA_LLM_BACKEND=groq

GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional per-provider model overrides. Each provider has a sensible default, and a
# model id belongs to exactly one of them - a Llama id sent to Gemini is a 404. Using
# the suffixed form lets all three stay configured while you switch between them.
#   uv run --directory core python -m aria --list-cloud-models
# ARIA_CLOUD_MODEL_GROQ=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# ARIA_CLOUD_MODEL_GOOGLE=gemini-3.5-flash
# ARIA_CLOUD_MODEL_OPENROUTER=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free

# --- Screen reading ----------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for ARIA_VISION_BACKEND=claude. The default backend is local Ollama
# and sends nothing anywhere.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ARIA_VISION_BACKEND=ollama

# --- Language ----------------------------------------------------------------
# auto (the default), en, or zh.
#
#   auto  she follows you, per turn. Speak English and she answers in English; speak
#         Chinese and she answers in Traditional Chinese (繁體中文), in a Mandarin
#         voice. Whisper detects the language, the chunker's script test picks the
#         voice, and the prompt ties the two together.
#   en    English only.
#   zh    Traditional Chinese only — she answers in Chinese even if you ask in English.
#
# Pinning removes the one decision detection can get wrong, which is worth having for
# a noisy room or a shared desk.
#
# ARIA_LANGUAGE=auto
# ARIA_ZH_VOICE=zf_xiaoxiao

# --- Overrides ---------------------------------------------------------------
# ARIA_VOICE=af_bella      # her English voice; ARIA_ZH_VOICE is the Chinese one
# ARIA_WAKE_WORD=aria

# Which local model Ollama runs. Any tag from https://ollama.com/library works, and
# Setup.bat downloads whatever this ends up being rather than a name written down
# separately - so changing it here and re-running setup is enough.
#
# The default is qwen3:8b. Her persona was written against the fine-tune below, which
# stays in character noticeably better; it is not the default because it is a community
# model with no content filtering, which should be a choice rather than a surprise.
# ARIA_LLM_MODEL=nexusriot/Qwen3.5-Uncensored-HauhauCS-Aggressive:9b
